{"name":"Wood Pigeon","hex":"#aabbcc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wood pigeon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several related species of pigeon in the family Columbidae, particularly the genus Columba:\n The common wood pigeon, Columba palumbus, an Old World species of pigeon.","The common wood pigeon, Columba palumbus, an Old World species of pigeon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood_pigeon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common wood pigeon","blocks":[{"text":"The common wood pigeon, also known simply as the wood pigeon, is a large pigeon native to the western Palearctic. It belongs to the genus Columba, which includes closely related species such as the rock dove. It has a flexible diet, feeding mainly on plant material, including cereals, and is therefore considered an agricultural pest. Wood pigeons are extensively hunted over much of their range, but this does not appear to have a major impact on their population numbers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Columba_palumbus_EM1B1397_%2827445478998%29.jpg/330px-Columba_palumbus_EM1B1397_%2827445478998%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_wood_pigeon"},{"title":"Columba (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"The bird genus Columba comprises a genus of medium to large pigeons. The terms \"dove\" and \"pigeon\" are used indiscriminately for smaller and larger Columbidae, respectively. Columba species are mostly termed \"pigeons\", and in many cases \"wood pigeons\", but some, are termed \"doves\". The rock dove has given rise to the majority of domesticated pigeon breeds, such as the racing pigeon and the fantail pigeon, some of which have become feral. Meanwhile, \"wood pigeon\" by itself usually means the common wood pigeon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/2018-03-22_Columba_oenas%2C_Jesmond_Dene_4.jpg/330px-2018-03-22_Columba_oenas%2C_Jesmond_Dene_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columba_(genus)"},{"title":"Wood Pigeon (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wood Pigeon, also known as The Ring-necked Dove, is a 1970 Iranian drama film, directed by Ali Hatami and starring Behrouz Vossoughi, Afarin Obeysi, Naser Malek Motiee, Zhaleh Olov, Hamideh Kheirabadi, and Bahman Mofid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/%D8%B7%D9%88%D9%82%DB%8C_%28%D9%BE%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%B1%29.jpg/330px-%D8%B7%D9%88%D9%82%DB%8C_%28%D9%BE%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%B1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_Pigeon_(film)"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Columba-palumbus-dist.png/500px-Columba-palumbus-dist.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Columba-palumbus-dist.png/1280px-Columba-palumbus-dist.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Columba-palumbus-dist.png/500px-Columba-palumbus-dist.